<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 14.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended December 14:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   154	   0.19     339800  52.33     6.43</p>
<p>Reliance	     188	   0.17     234750  44.13     4.72</p>
<p>ACC		   1010	   0.17	21170  21.38     0.88</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    320	   0.03	65700  21.02     4.89</p>
<p>Tata Power	   110	   0.14     164350  18.08     6.64</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 115	   0.15	61850   7.11     6.80</p>
<p>State Bank	   210	   0.19	23400   4.91     4.72</p>
<p>Andhra Valley	103	   0.13	41500   4.27     6.58</p>
<p>Bombay Dyeing	 95	   0.04	44450   4.22     2.20</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    158	   0.19	23400   3.70     6.27</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 5.18 percent on an annualised basis against 4.85 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Dec 7.</p>
